WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.300
Hi there.
嗨。

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.560
Welcome back for another interview with a cast member from The Paper.
欢迎再次收看由《The Paper》剧组成员参加的访谈。

3
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.300
And we should probably tell you, we watched the first four episodes.
我们或许应该告诉大家，我们看过了前四集。

4
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.740
We have watched them.
我们真的看过了。

5
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.020
It's so good.
真的太棒了。

6
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.260
It's really good.
确实非常好。

7
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.680
It's very hard not to say more, but we are not allowed.
很难忍住不剧透，但我们不能说。

8
00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.920
I think people are going to be happy.
我觉得大家会满意的。

9
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.020
I really do.
我是认真的。

10
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:21.700
I agree.
我同意。

11
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.640
I think it feels like The Office.
我觉得它很有《办公室》的感觉。

12
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.000
Like, it's very clear that this is the same universe.
就是那种很明显属于同一个宇宙的感觉。

13
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.340
Okay, that's all I think we can say.
好了，我觉得我们只能透露这么多了。

14
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.900
Yeah, we've probably said too much.
对，我们可能已经说得太多了。

15
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.700
Well, wait, I do want to say one more thing.
等一下，我还想说一件事。

16
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:33.060
Okay.
好。

17
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.940
I want to say that we are not sponsored by Peacock or NBC.
我想说的是，我们没有接受 Peacock 或 NBC 的赞助。

18
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.400
Yeah, no, we are not.
对，没有，我们真的没有。

19
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.360
I just want to say that because I just want people to know this is not an ad.
我只是想说明这一点，因为我想让大家知道这不是广告。

20
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.900
For Peacock or NBC.
针对 Peacock 或 NBC 的广告。

21
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:44.540
Correct.
没错。

22
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.060
Yeah, basically, here's what happened.
对，基本上事情是这样的。

23
00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:52.480
Greg invited Jenna and I to visit the set and to meet the caSt.
格雷格邀请詹娜和我去片场参观并见见演员们。

24
00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.100
And he shared with us some of our old crew was there.
他还告诉我们，我们以前的一些剧组成员也在那儿。

25
00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.120
We couldn't wait.
我们迫不及待地就去了。

26
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.560
And Greg has always been amazing to Office Ladies.
而且格雷格对《办公室女士》一直都非常好。

27
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.440
He's a huge supporter of the show.
他是我们节目的超级支持者。

28
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.280
And we went and went to the set.
于是我们就去了片场。

29
00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:14.000
And then he offered us an early sneak peek of the paper pilot and said maybe if we liked it, we could break it down because he said he's a huge fan of how we break down episodes.
然后他让我们提前先睹为快了《The Paper》的试播集，并说如果我们喜欢的话或许可以剖析一下，因为他说他非常喜欢我们剖析剧集的方式。

30
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.860
And so it all came together really organically.
所以这一切结合得非常自然。

31
00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.820
And I'm so glad we got to do this.
我很高兴我们能做这件事。

32
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:19.640
Me too.
我也是。

33
00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:24.140
And it just it meant so much to me that Greg trusts us.
格雷格能信任我们，对我和说真的意义重大。

34
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:24.760
Yes.
是的。

35
00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.480
With his new baby, basically, you know.
基本上就像是对待他的新宝贝一样，你懂的。

36
00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:28.020
Yeah.
对。

37
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.020
And I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

38
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.620
Greg, you're going to hear.
格雷格，你一定会听到这些的。

39
00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.020
Yes, you are.
你绝对会听到。

40
00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:33.660
We loved it.
我们真的很喜欢。

41
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:39.220
You know, lady, I do think that the rest of the cast is a little jealous that we got to see it early.
你知道吗，女士，我觉得其他演员对于我们能提前看到这一点有点嫉妒。

42
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:39.740
I do.
我真的觉得。

43
00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.080
I do.
确实如此。

44
00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:44.500
And I maybe am lording it over their heads a little bit.
而且我可能在他们面前稍微有点显摆。

45
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:45.040
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

46
00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.680
Did you tease Rain on your lunch?
你吃午饭时拿这事逗雷恩了吗？

47
00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.000
Were you like, Rain, guess what?
你会不会说，雷恩，你猜怎么着？

48
00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:48.900
Yes, I was like, Rain.
对，我就说，雷恩。

49
00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.240
I got to see it and you didn't.
我能看到，而你不能。

50
00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.580
I literally did.
我真的这么做了。

51
00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:52.540
I did.
我看了。

52
00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:58.200
I had lunch with Rain and I told him that I got to see it and that I wouldn't tell him anything.
我和雷恩吃午饭时告诉他我有幸看到了，而且我什么都不会告诉他。

53
00:01:58.360 --> 00:01:58.780
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

54
00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.240
I bet that made him crazy.
我敢打赌这把他急坏了。

55
00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:06.380
Well, listen, we are really excited because today we are sharing our interview with Sabrina Impecciatore.
好了，听着，我们真的很兴奋，因为今天我们要分享我们对萨布里纳·因佩恰托雷的采访。

56
00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.500
You might know her from season two of The White Lotus.
你可能从《白莲花度假村》第二季中认识她。

57
00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.640
She's fantastic.
她太棒了。

58
00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.500
And she is phenomenal in the paper.
她在《报社》里的表现简直惊艳。

59
00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.720
And her story of how she got her role on the paper is amazing.
她讲到自己是如何得到《报社》里的角色的，那个故事太神奇了。

60
00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:25.300
While we were talking to her, they actually called her to set during the interview, but I could have kept talking to her for an hour.
我们在跟她聊的时候，他们在采访中途实际上叫她去片场，但我真想跟她再聊一个小时。

61
00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:25.920
Truly.
真的。

62
00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.460
I, like, want to go on a road trip with her and just hear her talk.
我简直想跟她一起去公路旅行，就听她说话。

63
00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.000
Same.
我也是。

64
00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.760
I want to know even more things.
我还想知道更多的事情。

65
00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:32.140
Yeah.
是啊。

66
00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:33.200
All right.
好吧。

67
00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:37.720
Well, without further delay, here is our interview with Sabrina Impecciatore.
那么，废话不多说，这就是我们对萨布里纳·因佩恰托雷的采访。

68
00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.900
Well, it is so exciting to get to talk to you.
能有机会跟你聊聊，真的让人太激动了。

69
00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.740
Will you tell us your name and your character name?
能告诉我们你的名字和你的角色名字吗？

70
00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:47.400
Yes.
好的。

71
00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:54.100
Allora, my name is Sabrina Impecciatore and my character's name is Esmeralda Grand.
那么，我的名字是萨布里纳·因佩恰托雷，我角色的名字是埃斯梅拉达·格兰德。

72
00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:58.840
Can you tell us a little bit about what your character's story in the show is?
你能给我们简单讲讲你在剧中的角色经历吗？

73
00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.200
Oh, my God.
噢，我的天哪。

74
00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.120
I have no idea.
我完全不知道。

75
00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.140
What does she do?
她做了什么？

76
00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.040
What does she do in her job?
她在工作中做些什么？

77
00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.120
What doesn't she do?
有什么是她没做过的？

78
00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:16.980
I would say, because she does everything she can to just try to stay where she is.
我想说，因为她竭尽所能只是为了留在她现在的职位上。

79
00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:23.040
This is kind of crazy character.
这是一个有点疯狂的角色。

80
00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.800
Like, she could do anything.
比如，她什么都做得出来。

81
00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:29.100
To me, she's someone that needs to survive.
对我来说，她是一个需要生存的人。

82
00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:36.880
And so, but for her to survive, it's a very personal concept, you know?
所以，对她而言生存是一个非常个人的概念，你知道吗？

83
00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:50.380
So, every time she feels threatened by something, she uses anything she can, even the worst things possible, just to protect herself.
所以，每当她感到受到某种威胁时，她会利用任何能用的手段，甚至是可能最糟糕的手段，只为了保护自己。

84
00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:55.620
So, I see her like a little wild animal.
所以我把她看作是一只野性的小动物。

85
00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.140
And then she's the only Italian.
而且她是唯一的意大利人。

86
00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:04.060
She moved here and she doesn't want to leave.
她搬到了这里，而且不想离开。

87
00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:10.460
Like, she wants just to be here and keep living in this, in this country.
比如，她只想待在这里，继续在这个国家生活。

88
00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:18.860
And she works in this office, but she could actually do anything else because she's not a real journaliSt.
她在办公室工作，但实际上她什么别的工作都能做，因为她不是真正的记者。

89
00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:28.920
So, she is just someone that pretends to be anything because she just has to make it.
所以，她只是一个假装成各种身份的人，因为她必须混下去。

90
00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:33.900
Are you the only actual reporter at the paper?
你是报社里唯一真正的记者吗？

91
00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.120
Is that your job?
那是你的工作吗？

92
00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.300
No, not really.
不，其实不是。

93
00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:44.440
Like, my job was to be the editor-in-chief of TTT Online.
比如，我的工作是TTT网的主编。

94
00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:50.860
But then, and she was very happy about this, very proud.
但后来，她对此感到非常高兴，非常骄傲。

95
00:04:51.600 --> 00:05:00.660
And then this guy arrives, like the new, and she is literally kicked out of her office.
接着这个家伙来了，也就是新来的人，她字面意义上被赶出了自己的办公室。

96
00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:04.420
So, she struggles a lot because of that.
所以她为此挣扎了很久。

97
00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:15.240
And then she just tries to find her space in this new, you know, in this new hierarchy.
然后她只是试图在这个新的，你知道的，在这个新的层级结构中找到自己的空间。

98
00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:23.440
And so, of course, she is the one that wants always to be in front.
所以，当然，她总是那个想要冲在最前面的人。

99
00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:34.860
Like, she, she's also, to me, this is something that, because I've been creating this character with Greg and Michael and all the other writers.
比如，她，对我来说这也是因为我和格雷格、迈克尔以及所有其他编剧一起塑造了这个角色。

100
00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:40.320
Now, I was very, very inspired by, already by the sides during the audition.
从试镜时的台词开始，我就已经受到了非常非常大的启发。

101
00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:45.820
And so, then I decided to, I don't know, I didn't decide.
然后，我就决定去，我不知道，我其实没决定。

102
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:46.740
Things just arrived.
事情就这么发生了。

103
00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:55.720
So, to me, somehow, she thinks that through this documentary, one day maybe she could become a star.
所以，对我来说，不知为何，她觉得通过这部纪录片，也许有一天她能成为明星。

104
00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:01.700
So, she also uses the camera to suggest that idea.
所以，她也利用摄像机来暗示这种想法。

105
00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:12.320
That's why I decided to have this kind of hair, like a diva from the 40s, to suggest, hey, look at me.
这就是为什么我决定留这种发型，就像40年代的歌剧名伶一样，暗示着，嘿，看我。

106
00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.620
I'm a superstar, too.
我也是个超级巨星。

107
00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.240
And so, she acts like a star.
所以，她表现得像个明星。

108
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.960
She behaves like a star.
她举止像个明星。

109
00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:19.860
She, she thinks big.
她，她志存高远。

110
00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:21.700
She is, she's big.
她就是，她很大牌。

111
00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:27.460
The way she dresses, the way she acts, she is also very manipulative.
她的穿着，她的举止，她也很善于操纵他人。

112
00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.520
She uses everything, very manipulative.
她利用一切，非常善于操控。

113
00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.780
And, what a fun character.
而且，多么有趣的一个角色啊。

114
00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:34.120
I love her.
我爱死她了。

115
00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:35.940
I can't wait to watch this.
我迫不及待想看这个了。

116
00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:40.260
You know, it reminds me a lot of how Michael Scott loved the camera, right?
你知道，这让我想起了迈克尔·斯科特是如何喜爱摄像机的，对吧？

117
00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.560
And Andy, he thought he was going to be a big star.
还有安迪，他以为自己会成为一个大明星。

118
00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:46.240
He was very excited when the documentary airs.
纪录片播出时他非常兴奋。

119
00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.860
So, I sort of see a little bit of that theme.
所以，我从某种程度上看到了这样一点主题。

120
00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:54.840
Can you tell us about the audition, your process, and how you got your job on the paper?
你能跟我们聊聊试镜、你的流程，以及你是怎么得到《办公室》这份工作的吗？

121
00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.640
Yes, of course.
好的，没问题。

122
00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.580
So, that was, I have to be short because it's a long story.
所以，那是，我得简短点，因为这说来话长。

123
00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:03.760
But I was shooting a movie in Cape Town.
但我当时正在开普敦拍电影。

124
00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:09.740
I was in Cape Town, South Africa, since three months, far away from home and everything.
我在南非开普敦呆了三个月，远离家乡和一切。

125
00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:16.760
And I am literally entering in the flight, going back to Italy.
而我当时正准备登机回意大利。

126
00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:20.280
And I got a call from my agent from LA.
我接到了来自洛杉矶经纪人的电话。

127
00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.620
She said, Sabrina, did you, did you read the email?
她说，萨布丽娜，你，你看了邮件吗？

128
00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:24.780
I said, no.
我说，没有。

129
00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:25.400
What email?
什么邮件？

130
00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:26.240
I was packaging.
我正在打包行李。

131
00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:27.880
I was saying goodbye to the crew.
我在跟剧组人员告别。

132
00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.980
She had, do you have to read this email right now?
她说，你现在必须得看这封邮件吗？

133
00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:32.100
But I am almost flying.
但我马上就要起飞了。

134
00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:37.600
So, I read the email and there was the call for this audition.
于是我看了邮件，里面有这个试镜的通知。

135
00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:43.760
And they gave me 24 hours to prepare 11 pages in English.
他们只给我24小时用英语准备11页纸的剧本。

136
00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:50.260
24 hours was exactly the time of the flight back to Italy.
24小时刚好就是飞回意大利的飞行时间。

137
00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:56.600
But me, I felt, I cannot do an audition just coming out of the flight after.
但我觉得，我刚下飞机根本没办法做试镜。

138
00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:02.460
And so, I was telling my agent, please, please, try to get some time more.
所以，我告诉经纪人，求求你，求求你，尽量多争取一点时间。

139
00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.260
How can I learn these things?
我怎么能把这些东西背下来？

140
00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:05.340
I'm flying.
我在飞机上。

141
00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:06.320
I'm tired.
我很累。

142
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.080
I'm upset.
我很沮丧。

143
00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.880
And she said, I don't know if I can make it.
她说，我不知道能不能行。

144
00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.500
I'll write you.
我再写信给你。

145
00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.420
And so, now just go.
所以，现在你先登机吧。

146
00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:18.280
So, I flew for 10 hours and then I arrived in Doha.
于是，我飞了10个小时，然后到达了多哈。

147
00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:19.160
I can't remember.
我记不清了。

148
00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:23.240
I opened my email and she wrote me, we got one day more.
我打开邮箱，她写信告诉我，我们多争取到了一天时间。

149
00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:30.100
So, I was very excited, but still like, I can't make it.
所以，我非常兴奋，但同时又觉得，我还是做不到。

150
00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.020
Like, this is very long to learn.
就觉得，这太长了，根本背不下来。

151
00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:34.580
11 pages of monologues.
11页的独白。

152
00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:39.100
But I read this site and I felt in love.
但我看了这个网站，然后坠入爱河了。

153
00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:42.200
You know, it's like love at first sight.
你知道，就像一见钟情一样。

154
00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:45.380
I was like, oh my God, this is too brilliant.
我当时就想，天哪，这太棒了。

155
00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:46.960
This is too funny.
这太好笑了。

156
00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:50.320
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

157
00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:54.500
I had never saw The Office in my life.
我这辈子从来没看过《办公室》。

158
00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.000
I didn't know about this show.
我以前不知道这部剧。

159
00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:02.960
I was the only one on this planet that hadn't seen this show.
我是这个星球上唯一没看过这部剧的人。

160
00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:09.600
So, the first two episodes, I saw them on the flight from Cape Town to Rome.
所以，前两集我是从开普敦飞往罗马的航班上看的。

161
00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:10.080
Oh!
哦！

162
00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:15.740
And I felt like, oh my God, what a weird project.
然后我觉得，天哪，这是什么奇怪的项目。

163
00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:19.160
That doesn't look like anything familiar.
看起来跟见过的任何东西都不一样。

164
00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:20.920
That's so weird.
太诡异了。

165
00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.680
And this acting is so believable.
而且这演技太逼真了。

166
00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:24.940
It looks really like it.
看起来真的很像那么回事。

167
00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:26.780
And the light is so bad.
而且光线这么差。

168
00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:28.040
I'm going to be so ugly.
我会显得好丑。

169
00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:31.120
That was the main concern.
那是我最主要的担忧。

170
00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:34.880
So, then I arrived in Rome.
于是，后来我到了罗马。

171
00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:37.480
After three months, I don't see my mom and nothing.
三个月没见我妈，什么都没做。

172
00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.000
But I called my mom and said, mom, forget about me.
但我给我妈打电话说，妈，别管我了。

173
00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:42.520
Have an audition tomorrow.
我明天有个试镜。

174
00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:45.120
So, we can't see.
所以，我们见不了面。

175
00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:45.600
We can't.
我们见不了。

176
00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:48.980
So, I spend all night long to study the sites.
所以我花了一整晚的时间研究这些片段。

177
00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:51.720
I find an American girl.
我找了一个美国女孩。

178
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:52.860
It's a long story.
说来话长。

179
00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.840
That she comes to my place and we study, study, study, study.
她来到我家，然后我们不停地学习、学习、学习、学习。

180
00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:02.480
And then I do this Zoom meeting with all my luggages looking at me.
然后我带着我所有的行李，它们看着我，进行了这场 Zoom 会议。

181
00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:03.580
You know, the luggages.
你知道，那些行李。

182
00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:04.800
I couldn't touch the luggage.
我碰都不能碰那些行李。

183
00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:05.540
I couldn't open that.
我没法打开它们。

184
00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:06.440
They were there.
它们就摆在那儿。

185
00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:11.540
And I did this Zoom meeting with Greg, with Michael, with the casting director, with the
我跟格雷格、迈克尔、选角导演还有

186
00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:12.020
producers.
制片人们开了一场 Zoom 会议。

187
00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:14.300
There were six, seven people there.
那里有六、七个人。

188
00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:17.820
And I said, okay, let's go.
然后我想，好吧，开始吧。

189
00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.120
And I forgot all the lines.
结果我把台词全忘光了。

190
00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.600
Of course, the memory was not solid enough.
当然，记忆还不够扎实。

191
00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:29.440
So, I started the scenes with the correct lines.
所以，我用正确的台词开始了表演。

192
00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:34.660
But after a couple of lines, I completely invented everything else.
但演了莫约两句台词后，剩下的我完全是现编的。

193
00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:35.420
Like, whoa.
就像是，哇。

194
00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:38.100
So, I was improvising, improvising, improvising.
所以，我一直在即兴发挥，即兴发挥，即兴发挥。

195
00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:39.800
And I didn't hear a sound.
而且我一点声音都没听到。

196
00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.520
So, I said, this is going very bad.
所以我心想，这下要砸了。

197
00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:43.120
But it's okay.
不过没关系。

198
00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:43.620
I'll keep going.
我继续演下去。

199
00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:47.080
I kept going for 40 minutes, I think.
我想我足足演了40分钟。

200
00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:47.960
45 minutes.
45分钟。

201
00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.500
And then they said, stop.
然后他们说，停。

202
00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:52.700
And they all appeared.
然后他们全员露面了。

203
00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:55.820
I had understood that they had mute themselves.
我以为他们把自己全静音了。

204
00:10:56.180 --> 00:11:01.660
They said, Sabrina, you really made us laugh a lot.
他们说，萨布丽娜，你真的把我们逗得哈哈大笑。

205
00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:06.080
But you didn't remember nothing.
但你什么都没记住。

206
00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:12.340
And they said, could you do this again in two days?
然后他们说，两天后你能再来一次吗？

207
00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:13.660
What the fuck?
搞什么鬼？

208
00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:14.580
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

209
00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.500
I said, really?
我说，真的吗？

210
00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:19.240
Like, after three months, I'm not even.
就好像，过了三个月，我甚至都……

211
00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:19.700
Okay.
好吧。

212
00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:24.220
So, two days after, I did this again.
于是，两天后，我又来了一次。

213
00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:27.620
But with all the memory and everything.
但带着所有的记忆和一切。

214
00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:33.200
And actually, I sent a self-tape with all the scenes.
其实，我发了一段包含所有场景的自录试镜视频。

215
00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:34.320
I was very inspired.
我当时灵感爆棚。

216
00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.940
Like, I was very inspired.
真的，我灵感爆棚。

217
00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:38.980
I felt like I was a channel and things were just arriving.
我感觉自己像个灵媒，各种灵感源源不断地涌现。

218
00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:41.500
And I was having so much fun in that audition.
而且我在那场试镜里玩得太开心了。

219
00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.460
And then I sent it.
然后我把它发了出去。

220
00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.860
And then for a month, I don't hear from anybody.
接着整整一个月，我音讯全无。

221
00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:49.820
So, I thought, okay, it's not working.
所以我想，好吧，没戏了。

222
00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:59.440
I was very sad because in the meanwhile, I was watching The Office and I was like, oh, my God, this project is the most brilliant project I've seen.
我很伤心，因为在这期间，我一直在看《办公室》，心想，天哪，这个项目是我见过最才华横溢的项目。

223
00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:04.460
It was so incredibly intelligent and real funny.
它太不可思议地聪明且真正好笑。

224
00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:12.280
You know, when you laugh, you laugh with your brain, with your heart, with your everything.
你知道的，当你大笑时，你是用大脑、用心灵、用你的全身心在笑。

225
00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:13.380
You're really laughing.
你是发自内心地在笑。

226
00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:20.580
And then, incredibly enough, after one month, I got another role.
然后，难以置信的是，一个月后，我得到了另一个角色。

227
00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:24.960
A big, big role, like a very big, important project.
一个很大很重要的角色，是一个非常盛大、重要的项目。

228
00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:28.140
So, I was very happy because I said, oh, my God.
所以我非常高兴，因为我说，天哪。

229
00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:32.000
So, I was jumping on the air because of this other role.
因为这个别的角色，我高兴得手舞足蹈。

230
00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:36.500
Like, I was crying because it was really something I loved.
就像，我都哭了，因为这真的是我热爱的东西。

231
00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:41.920
And so, it was like midnight because from Italy to America.
当时大约是半夜，因为从意大利到美国有时差。

232
00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:44.860
It was midnight and all my team called me from the U.S.
正值半夜，我所有的美国团队成员都打电话给我。

233
00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:46.660
Sabrina, you got that role.
萨布丽娜，你拿下那个角色了。

234
00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:47.040
Wow.
哇。

235
00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.460
So, I have fun.
所以我玩得很开心。

236
00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.360
I drink with all my friends.
我和所有朋友一起喝酒。

237
00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:52.060
We celebrate.
我们庆祝。

238
00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:52.640
We toss.
我们干杯。

239
00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:53.200
Blah, blah, blah.
巴拉巴拉巴拉。

240
00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:54.380
Then, I go back home.
然后，我回家了。

241
00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:55.880
It's 4 o'clock a.m.
当时是凌晨4点。

242
00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:58.880
And I feel, beep, beep, beep, beep.
然后我手机一直响，哔，哔，哔，哔。

243
00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:04.500
From my team, Sabrina, you also got the role from The Office.
来自我的团队：萨布丽娜，你还拿下了《办公室》的角色。

244
00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:07.280
Oh, in the same day.
噢，在同一天。

245
00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:08.760
You found out in the same day.
你在同一天知道了这一切。

246
00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:09.180
Day.
同一天。

247
00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:10.220
Oh, my goodness.
噢，天呐。

248
00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:11.600
That was actually the same night.
那其实是同一个晚上。

249
00:13:11.820 --> 00:13:12.380
Right, right, right.
对，对，对。

250
00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:15.480
So, that was so crazy.
所以，那简直太疯狂了。

251
00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.340
I couldn't sleep, of course.
我当然睡不着。

252
00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.520
I was in my back, like, what's happening?
我躺在床上，心想：这是怎么回事？

253
00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:21.860
What am I doing?
我在干什么？

254
00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:22.740
What's going to happen?
接下来会发生什么？

255
00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:23.600
What can I do?
我能做些什么？

256
00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:27.900
So, I had just a couple of days to take a decision.
所以，我只有几天时间来做决定。

257
00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:30.280
And I was desperate, really.
而且我真的很绝望。

258
00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:32.420
You had to choose between the two?
你必须在这两者之间做出选择？

259
00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:33.960
You couldn't do all.
你不能全都要吗？

260
00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:34.700
No, you couldn't do both.
对，你不能两样都要。

261
00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:35.520
They were exactly.
它们简直是……

262
00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:38.920
And they were two things that I really loved.
而且这是两件我都非常热爱的事。

263
00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:42.680
So, I was really, really, really desperate, to be honeSt.
所以，说实话，我真的、真的、真的很绝望。

264
00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:44.820
You want to know the truth?
你想知道真相吗？

265
00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:49.960
When I took the decision, I cried for six hours.
当我做出决定时，我哭了六个小时。

266
00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.620
And it was a long time I wasn't crying.
而且我已经很久没有哭过了。

267
00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:58.420
But I cried for six hours because I thought, this is how my life crazy, my crazy life is.
但我哭了六个小时，因为我想，我的生活就是这么疯狂，我这疯狂的生活啊。

268
00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:06.060
I have to say no to something that is unbelievable to me because some other thing that is unbelievable is happening.
我不得不对一件让我难以置信的事说不，因为另一件同样难以置信的事正在发生。

269
00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:11.160
So, and then Greg and Michael called me.
然后，格雷格和迈克尔给我打电话了。

270
00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:18.000
I will never forget that call because at first they had asked me, Sabrina, can you learn an American accent?
我永远不会忘记那个电话，因为一开始他们问我：“萨布丽娜，你能学会美式口音吗？”

271
00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:22.540
And me, perfectly lying, I said, of course I can.
而我，面不改色地撒了谎：“我当然可以。”

272
00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:25.320
But I was so scared.
但我其实吓坏了。

273
00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.700
I said, how can I learn an American accent so fastly?
我心想：我怎么可能这么快就学会美式口音？

274
00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:38.560
Then they called me, they said, Sabrina, after watching your audition, we cannot imagine any other actor, actress doing this role.
然后他们打电话给我，说：“萨布丽娜，看完你的试镜后，我们无法想象还有哪个演员能演这个角色。”

275
00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:40.420
So, and we also love your accent.
所以，而且我们也超爱你的口音。

276
00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:41.540
It's so charming.
太迷人了。

277
00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:43.660
God, take it, take it.
天哪，接下它，接下它。

278
00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:45.260
And this is how it happened.
事情就是这样发生的。

279
00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:49.400
Well, I, what a story.
哇，真是个故事。

280
00:14:49.720 --> 00:15:02.240
And, you know, this is one of the great things about working with Greg Daniels is that he attaches to a performer, to an actor, and he really respects the craft of the actor.
而且，你知道，与格雷格·丹尼尔斯合作最棒的一点在于，他会与表演者、与演员建立连接，而且他非常尊重演员的表演艺术。

281
00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:09.580
And he wants to draw parts of you into the character that he had in mind.
他希望将你身上的一些特质融入他构思的角色中。

282
00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:12.380
And there's such a collaboration there.
那种合作感真的很棒。

283
00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:18.940
And you get to be a part of, you know, you said you felt like you were channeling something.
你可以成为其中的一部分，就像你说的，你感觉自己好像在传导某种能量。

284
00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:27.740
And Greg is, he's humble enough to invite that kind of collaboration.
而格雷格非常谦逊，愿意邀请这种合作。

285
00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:28.700
Yeah.
是的。

286
00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.420
He loves creative collaboration.
他热爱创意合作。

287
00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:33.660
I always felt like we were building something together.
我总是觉得我们是在一起构筑某些东西。

288
00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:38.860
You know, I didn't have just this boss telling me, your character does this and you do this.
你知道，不只是一个老板对我说：‘你的角色就这样，你得这么演。’

289
00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:41.880
It was a conversation and you're part of that.
这是一个对话过程，而你是其中的一部分。

290
00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.540
What a great story.
多棒的故事啊。

291
00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:45.520
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

292
00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:58.240
What has it been like now working on the show?
现在参演这部剧的感觉怎么样？

293
00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:00.820
A lot of girls.
有很多女孩。

294
00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:08.560
When I got this role done, of course, I couldn't sleep for many weeks because I was very scared.
当我拿下这个角色后，当然，我连续好几个星期都睡不着，因为我非常害怕。

295
00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:09.460
I was terrified.
我吓坏了。

296
00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:13.180
Because the quality of the acting was so high level.
因为演员的演技水平太高了。

297
00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:18.200
I said, I cannot, I will never join that level.
我想，我做不到，我永远也达不到那个水准。

298
00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:24.460
And watching Steve Carell's work, for example, to me was epiphanic.
举个例子，看史蒂夫·卡瑞尔的表演对我来说简直是一次顿悟。

299
00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:36.700
Was, I thought, this guy is one of the biggest artists on this planet because he's able to make me laugh in a very sophisticated way.
当时我想，这家伙是这个星球上最伟大的艺术家之一，因为他能够以一种非常精致的方式逗笑我。

300
00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:38.840
And everything is in his eyes.
而且一切都在他的眼神里。

301
00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:40.680
He has this innocence.
他有一种纯真。

302
00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:45.020
And there was something really incredible about him.
而且他身上有一种非常了不起的特质。

303
00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:55.860
So, because I believe in energies and everything, I got to know that he was playing Uncle Vanya in New York in Broadway.
所以，因为我相信能量之类的东西，我了解到他在纽约百老汇出演《万尼亚舅舅》。

304
00:16:56.580 --> 00:17:01.240
And I took a flight to go to meet him from Rome.
于是我从罗马坐飞机去见他。

305
00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:03.400
I got a flight to see the show.
我坐飞机去看演出。

306
